  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Occurred during Community Meetup in the VR Awards World (The conjoined one shown for community meetup. However, the teleports I saw this occur on are also existent in VR Awards Act 4). A friend would leave his world camera behind to watch us as he was ahead of the rest of us. Then later on when we teleported to his room (due to the nature of the world), his ik kept slowed like he was very distant, even though he was right next to us, and we couldn't hear him. This is until he turned off the world camera. Then his ik turned back to normal and we could hear him again. This also happened to myself, where I left my world camera, and then after the next teleport, a friend could not hear me and my ik was that same slowness, until I turned my camera back to the next mode. Then he could hear me and see me move properly again. Originally we thought it might be sync due to the world, but the maker said there wasn't a lot of sync there, and both times it occurred, it was fixed by bringing the world camera back.",
